snippet.description:
Cristiano Ronaldo retired from Portugal on Thursday, and within hours, the comment section under his video turned into a who's who of football. Vinícius Júnior: "Forever number one." Neymar, one word: "Legend." Rio Ferdinand: "It was a movie, bro." And Pepe, the man who stood next to him at Real Madrid and for Portugal: "It was more than football. Thank you for everything, Cris."

And that was just the start. Portugal's president posted. So did the prime minister, and so did Guinness World Records. One old teammate called him the best of all time, then admitted they "often disagreed." The manager who dropped him at the 2022 World Cup sent a message. Rio made a whole video, and admitted he didn't see it coming. And the name everyone keeps checking for? Lionel Messi. A month ago, Ronaldo wrote under Messi's goodbye post. By the end of this, you'll know if he's returned the favour. Right. Let's get into it.
@cristiano #ronaldo #cristianoronaldo #portugal #retirement #retire

